<title>TURKEY: Cargill trader sees corn breaking below $3/bushel.</title>
<headline>Cargill trader sees corn breaking below $3/bushel.</headline>
<dateline>ANTALYA, Turkey 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. corn futures prices, currently around $3.11 a bushel, are likely to break below $3.00 a bushel and $2.75 is not excluded, a Cargill grains trader said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Fausto Filice of Cargill International in Geneva told a grains conference that the U.S. corn crop could be bigger and demand, particularly for export, lower than the U.S. governmennt currently forecasts.</p>
</text>
